# xreserve::attester_admin
#
# FAUCET(01)-owned deposit-attester allowlist admin (P5-01 set_attester + RBAC-foundation slice):
# the ATTEST_ADMIN-gated `set_attester` setter that writes the xReserveAttesters allowlist — the
# on-chain write completing the D5d read seam (attestation_verify.masm:95-119, R-MINT-13). The slot
# this setter co-owns is named by attestation_verify.masm:26
# (word("xusdc::xreserve::attester_admin::xreserve_attesters")). Module home + flat path per D-1A
# (CANONICAL-OWNERSHIP-MAP.md:59). Loop history: crates/xusdc-encoding/TEST-LEDGER-01-MINT-SHELL.md.
#
# SCAFFOLD (executing-red commit): `set_attester` is a named placeholder that traps
# ERR_SET_ATTESTER_UNIMPLEMENTED so the red suite assembles and every test reaches execute().await
# (red at runtime, never a compile error). The green commit replaces the body with the real gate +
# write (assert_authorized -> assert_not_paused -> set_map_item) and drops this error const.

# ERRORS
# =================================================================================================

# Executing-red placeholder trap; removed when the real body lands (green commit).
const ERR_SET_ATTESTER_UNIMPLEMENTED = "set_attester is not yet implemented"

# PUBLIC INTERFACE
# =================================================================================================

#! ATTEST_ADMIN-gated setter for the xReserveAttesters allowlist: enables (enabled = 1) or disables
#! (enabled = 0) a deposit attester keyed by its pubkey commitment. The §5.5 setter — it trusts the
#! caller's commitment Word verbatim and does NOT recompute it from a raw pubkey.
#!
#! Inputs:  [PK_COMMITMENT, enabled, pad(11)]
#! Outputs: [pad(16)]
#!
#! Where:
#! - PK_COMMITMENT is the Poseidon2 pubkey commitment (the xReserveAttesters map key).
#! - enabled is 1 to allowlist the attester (write the enabled marker) or 0 to remove it (write
#!   EMPTY_WORD).
#!
#! Panics if:
#! - the note sender does not hold ATTEST_ADMIN (ERR_SENDER_LACKS_ROLE, green commit).
#! - the faucet is paused (ERR_PAUSABLE_IS_PAUSED, green commit).
#!
#! Invocation: call
#!
#! SCAFFOLD: unconditional trap (ERR_SET_ATTESTER_UNIMPLEMENTED) until the green commit. Uses
#! `push.1 assertz` (NOT `push.0 assert`) so this proc's MAST root differs from the structurally
#! identical `mint_deny_guard::check_policy` — error messages are MAST decorators, not part of the
#! root, so two `push.0 assert.err=…` procs would collide and the deny-guard `dynexec` would surface
#! THIS error. The real body (green commit) is structurally distinct and needs no such guard.
pub proc set_attester
    push.1 assertz.err=ERR_SET_ATTESTER_UNIMPLEMENTED
end
